      "message": "**Issue:**\nThe assertion validating the test setup could be clearer.\n\n```cpp\nzassert_true(\n    (FP_SENSOR_IMAGE_OFFSET + size) \u003c\u003d (sizeof(fp_buffer) + 1),\n    \"Test setup: Underflow condition not met; check your constants.\");\n\n```\n\nWhile the math is technically correct (verifying that the subtraction yielding `offset` didn\u0027t wrap around below zero), the phrasing \"Underflow condition not met\" is slightly confusing. It suggests the test *wants* an underflow to happen, rather than asserting that an underflow *did not* happen during setup.\n\n**Suggestion:**\nReword the assertion message to clearly state the invariant being enforced:\n\n```cpp\nzassert_true(\n    (sizeof(fp_buffer) + 1) \u003e\u003d (FP_SENSOR_IMAGE_OFFSET + size),\n    \"Test setup: Offset calculation wrapped. FP_SENSOR_IMAGE_OFFSET + size must be \u003c\u003d sizeof(fp_buffer) + 1.\");\n\n```\n\nThis makes it immediately obvious to future maintainers why the assertion exists: to ensure the derived `offset` remains a valid positive integer.",
